# Supabase Rules

## Workflow

```bash
supabase migration new <name>   # never edit pushed migrations
supabase db push
supabase db reset               # local rebuild
supabase start
```

After schema changes:

```bash
supabase gen types typescript --linked > frontend/src/types/supabase.ts
```

## Tables & view

| Object | Notes |
|--------|-------|
| `profiles` | Auto-created by `handle_new_user` trigger on `auth.users` — never client INSERT |
| `forms` | Owner RLS; `updated_at` via `forms_set_updated_at` trigger |
| `form_responses` | anon INSERT only when parent published |
| `generation_jobs` | Owner-scoped job status |
| `public_forms` | View: `id, public_slug, title, description, definition` where `status = 'published'` |

## Invariants

- `forms_published_requires_slug`: `public_slug IS NOT NULL` when `status = 'published'`.
- Respondents: SELECT `public_forms` only — do not grant anon on `forms`.
- New respondent-visible columns → `ALTER VIEW public_forms`, not looser RLS on `forms`.

## Storage

### `sketches` (owner sketch uploads)

- Private; 10 MB; MIME jpeg/png/webp.
- Path: `sketches/{auth.uid()}/{form_id_or_filename}.{ext}`
- RLS: first segment = `auth.uid()::text`
- Backend reads via service role (no user read policy for API).

### `response-uploads` (respondent `file_upload` fields)

- Private; 10 MB; MIME jpeg/png/webp + `application/pdf`.
- Path: `response-uploads/{form_id}/{uuid}.{ext}`
- anon INSERT gated on published form (`public_forms`); owner SELECT/DELETE.
- Answer JSON: `{ path, name, size, mime }` — not raw file bytes in Postgres.

## Security definer

`handle_new_user` runs as SECURITY DEFINER — keep migration changes reviewed.

## Linked project

See `supabase/.temp/linked-project.json` for project ref (local dev).
